==============================================================================================
(B) Structural facts about a(m)=meas(S7(AP_m)) for the subset-domination route
==============================================================================================
  (B1) a(m) non-decreasing for m=1..22: True.  First strict increase at m=6.
       a(m)=0 for m<=6 (PROVED B1 of THM-536: <7 partial sums can't cover Z/7).
  (B2) a(m) < 1 for all finite m (the all-covered theta-set is open, misses boundary);
       a(22)=0.82100. Sequence is increasing toward 1.

  N*(k) = max span certified by pointwise domination = max{N : a(N+1) <= cap_k}:
    k= 8: cap_k= 2243/5880 (0.3815)  N*=7  a(N*+1)=0.3272<=cap  a(N*+2)=0.4162>cap
    k= 9: cap_k= 1979/4004 (0.4943)  N*=8  a(N*+1)=0.4162<=cap  a(N*+2)=0.5045>cap
